I. Adding the meta-raspberrypi-rt layer to your build
=================================================

Run 'bitbake-layers add-layer meta-raspberrypi-rt'

II. Misc
========

The meta-raspberrypi-rt layer provides support for building a real-time Linux system using the PREEMPT_RT patchset
for the Raspberry Pi 4 (64-bit) with Yocto Project (Kirkstone branch).

Features include:

- PREEMPT_RT enabled Linux kernel (5.15.x)
- Real-time image recipe (`image-rt`)
- Support for `openssh`, `rsyslog`, `rt-tests`, `gdbserver`, `wiringpi` 
- Minimal set of enabled drivers and services to optimize real-time performance
- Ethernet, Serial and USB support
- Kernel configuration fragments and SCCs for easy PREEMPT_RT customization
- Output image in WIC format (wic.bz2, wic.bmap) for flashing with `bmaptool` or `dd`

This layer is designed to be used in conjunction with `poky`, `meta-openembedded`, and `meta-raspberrypi`.

And optionally configure CPU isolation and kernel boot args in `config.txt` and `cmdline.txt` for better real-time performance.
